From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: snoc: use one predicate for the irq
 disable/enable pair

ath10k_snoc_hif_stop() skips ath10k_snoc_irq_disable() when
ATH10K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH is set, but ath10k_snoc_hif_start() skips the
matching ath10k_snoc_irq_enable() on a different flag,
ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_RECOVERY. ath10k_core_restart() sets only the former,
so a restart-initiated stop leaves the CE interrupt lines armed across
ath10k_hw_power_off(); a late CE interrupt then services a register
access against an unclocked block, which on msm8998 stalls the config
NoC with no bus error. It is also the source of the "Unbalanced
enable for IRQ" storm on every firmware restart. Use the same
predicate on both sides of the balance.
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c
index 8c3871692800..184fdc56d53d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c
@@ -925,7 +925,9 @@ static void ath10k_snoc_buffer_cleanup(struct ath10k *ar)
 
 static void ath10k_snoc_hif_stop(struct ath10k *ar)
 {
-	if (!test_bit(ATH10K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ar->dev_flags))
+	struct ath10k_snoc *ar_snoc = ath10k_snoc_priv(ar);
+
+	if (!test_bit(ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ar_snoc->flags))
 		ath10k_snoc_irq_disable(ar);
 
 	ath10k_core_napi_sync_disable(ar);
